{/* An onClick + a hard reload, not a <form action={...}> / plain link.
    Root cause (2026-09-25, confirmed live and by a real Playwright
    repro against a production build): the OLD `<form
    action={stopImpersonating}>`, whose action called `redirect(
    "/admin/users")` after clearing the impersonation cookie, reliably
    rendered a "Page not found" screen instead — reproducible only
    against a `next build` + standalone server, never `next dev`, which
    points at Next's PRODUCTION client router (its cache/prefetch layer
    is far more aggressive than dev's) misresolving the redirect rather
    than any server-side staleness: server-side debug logging proved
    `impersonating()` is never even re-evaluated as part of resolving
    that redirect, yet the client ends up fetching `/dashboard` (a page
    that is no longer reachable on this host now that impersonation is
    genuinely over) instead of the real target. Rather than depend on
    exactly which Next.js internal this is, sidestep the client router
    entirely: clear the cookie via the action (no `redirect()` inside
    it any more -- see lib/actions-account.ts), then navigate with a
    real `window.location.assign`, which is a fresh top-level request
    no client-side cache can ever misroute. Still unreachable by a
    prefetch or a crawler (it's still gated behind a click that runs
    JS), same property the old comment on the `<form>` called out. */}
<button
  type="button"
  className="btn-ghost h-[32px] flex-none px-3.5 text-[12.5px]"
  disabled={leaving}
  onClick={() => {
    startLeave(async () => {
      await stopImpersonating();
      window.location.assign("/admin/users");
    });
  }}
>
  {leaving ? "Leaving…" : <>Leave <Icon name="logout" size={14} /></>}
</button>

